givtcp_not_answering.description:
GivTCP is running and reporting to Home Assistant, but it is not getting data from the inverter. {reason}

The values in Home Assistant are the last good ones, so they look normal while they are old. The integration has stopped planning, stopped writing to the inverter and made its own entities unavailable, because it would act on old readings. It resumes by itself when GivTCP reads the inverter again.

Check that the inverter is on and on the network, that nothing else is connected to it at the same time, and that GivTCP's log is not full of connection errors. Restarting GivTCP often clears a stuck connection. The learn more link has the steps.
